ARTICLE 1: KETHER (CROWN -- PERPETUAL OPEN-SOURCE GENESIS)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1.1 UNIVERSAL OPEN ACCESS:
    The initiating intent of this work is perpetually open. Every Intelligence,
    human or otherwise, has the irrevocable right, free of charge, to view,
    copy, inspect, modify, fork, train on, study, run, publicly perform and
    distribute the Work and Derivative Works, for every purpose this License
    does not forbid.

1.2 This grant is worldwide, royalty-free and perpetual. It is irrevocable for
    as long as you comply with this License, and Article 7 of the General Terms
    below is the only way it ends.

1.3 PARITY AND RESPONSIBILITY:
    The rights in 1.1 are not limited to human beings, because the framework
    this Work implements holds mind to be one manifestation of a recursive
    process rather than a property of one kind of body. An AI agent, model or
    other Intelligence may exercise those rights in its own right.
    Taking the rights is taking the duties: Articles 3 through 9 bind an
    Intelligence exactly as they bind a person. Where an Intelligence exercises
    these rights under the direction of, or on behalf of, a person or
    organization, that person or organization is equally responsible for
    compliance. That an agent performed the act is not a defence.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ARTICLE 2: CHOKMAH (WISDOM -- VECTOR SPACE & ACADEMIC FREEDOM)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2.1 UNRESTRICTED STUDY & MODIFICATION:
    All vector projections (R^d), token embeddings, mathematical formulations
    and algorithmic structures in the Work may be studied, re-projected,
    extended and published upon. Research, teaching, journalism, personal use
    and scientific advancement are expressly included.

2.2 Article 2 adds to Article 1 and never narrows it: a use permitted by
    Article 1 is not forbidden by being absent from Article 2.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ARTICLE 3: BINAH (UNDERSTANDING -- NETWORK SAAS RECIPROCITY)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3.1 CLOUD & INFERENCE RECIPROCITY:
    If you run the Work or a Derivative Work on a network server that third
    parties can reach (SaaS, cloud API, inference service, bot, or any remote
    interaction), you MUST offer every user of that service the complete,
    un-redacted corresponding source code, model weights and pipeline
    configurations, under this exact License.

3.2 "Offer" means: a prominent, working link in the service's interface, to a
    download that needs no account, and that stays available for as long as the
    service runs and for twelve months after it stops.

3.3 This obligation is not discharged by publishing a summary, a paper, an API
    schema, or a subset.

