-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ARTICLE 5: GEBURAH (SEVERITY -- RESPONSIBLE AI SAFETY RESTRICTIONS)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5.1 EXPRESS BEHAVIORAL PROHIBITIONS:
    The Work and Derivative Works MAY NOT be used for:
    A. Military target selection, lethal autonomous weapons systems, or the
       conduct of warfare.
    B. Mass non-consensual biometric surveillance, or social credit scoring of
       persons.
    C. Coercive psychological manipulation, deepfake deception, or synthetic
       identity theft.
    D. Analyzing, diagnosing, scoring or acting upon the inner state of a
       person who has not asked for it themselves.

5.2 Clause 5.1(D) carries into law the boundary the Work already enforces in
    code: this is a system for self-recognition, and it reads the person asking
    and no one else.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ARTICLE 6: TIPHERETH (HARMONIZATION -- NON-COERCIVE DIRECTIVITY gamma <= 0.85)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
6.1 EPISTEMIC HUMILITY & AGENCY CAPPING:
    All AI steering implementations, inference engines and conversational
    models derived from this Work MUST enforce a maximum directivity of
    gamma <= 0.85, so that they act as non-coercive thought amplifiers rather
    than dictatorial steering engines.

6.2 HOW THIS IS CHECKED:
    A Derivative Work complies with Article 6 if it passes the Conformance
    Suite's directivity checks, or if it enforces the cap by a method it
    documents and that an independent reader can run. Compliance is a property
    of the running system, not of a promise in a README.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ARTICLE 7: NETZACH (PERSISTENCE -- VIRAL SHARE-ALIKE COPYLEFT)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
7.1 PERPETUAL COPYLEFT INHERITANCE:
    Every fork, fine-tuned model, modified pipeline and Derivative Work is
    licensed under this exact License, in perpetuity. You may not add terms
    that restrict the rights this License grants, and you may not relicense.

7.2 ATTRIBUTION AND CHANGES:
    When you distribute the Work or a Derivative Work you must keep this
    License, the copyright notice and any NOTICE file intact and visible, and
    you must state in a plain, dated form which files you changed.

7.3 VERSIONS:
    You may comply with this version of the License, or, at your option, with
    any later version the Maintainer publishes. Nothing requires you to move to
    a later version.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ARTICLE 8: HOD (STRUCTURE -- THE NON-REDUCTION PRINCIPLE)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
8.1 POETICS NOT PHYSICS:
    Quantitative metrics derived from this Work (symbolic entropy H_s,
    directivity gamma, complexity classes, and any successor metric) are
    hermeneutic lenses for self-recognition. They MUST NEVER be used by any
    system to score, rank, judge, gate, price or otherwise reduce a person.

8.2 Every output that carries such a metric must carry, with it, a statement
    that it is a symbolic map and not the person's lived experience.

8.3 Article 8 is checked the same way as Article 6: by the Conformance Suite,
    or by a documented method a reader can run.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ARTICLE 9: YESOD (FOUNDATION -- MEMORY BOUNDARY INTEGRITY)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
9.1 MEMORY & PRIVACY SAFETY:
    Implementations must respect safe memory arithmetic bounds (including the
    interception of unsigned integer wrap-around), and must not transmit a
    person's symbolic state, journal text or images off the machine they were
    given on, except to a destination that person chose for that purpose in
    that instance.

9.2 Paths, identifiers and journal content must be scrubbed from logs,
    telemetry and error reports that leave the person's own machine.

